From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: honor the mmap offset in the GEM fault handler

msm_gem_fault() takes the page index from the fault address relative to
vma->vm_start and never looks at the mapping's page offset. That is only
right while every mapping starts at page 0 of the object and is never
split. It breaks:

- dma-buf mmap at a nonzero offset: dma_buf_mmap_internal() allows
  vm_pgoff + pages <= size, drm_gem_prime_mmap() adds the fake offset, so
  vm_pgoff = fake offset + N, but the fault maps page 0 at the start of
  the mapping instead of page N (seen with Turnip-exported OPAQUE_FD and
  DMA_BUF memory on Adreno 740: an mmap at offset N shows offset 0);
- the tail left by munmap of a mapping's head, and a sub-range moved by
  mremap: the VMA's vm_pgoff moves along, the fault ignores it, and any
  page not yet faulted in shows the wrong page.

vmf->pgoff already holds the page's position in the mmap offset space
(linear_page_index()); take the object's fake offset back off, as TTM does
in ttm_bo_vm_fault_reserved(). A whole-object mapping at offset 0 gets the
same index as before (vm_pgoff equals the fake offset). Fail an index past
the end of the object with SIGBUS instead of reading past the pages array.

PB-OS's 0611 (project-barry/pb-os 55c2d28f76, external-and-mods/
kernel-sm8650/sm8550/patches, by lavachemist; tried by PB-OS on a Retroid
Pocket 6 with a 7.3 test kernel: their offset-mapping test went from 16
failures to none). Ours: the line it replaces is 7.2's open-coded
(vmf->address - vma->vm_start) >> PAGE_SHIFT, not linear_page_delta();
the change is the same. Not yet tried on a Thor.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
@@ -450,8 +450,18 @@ static vm_fault_t msm_gem_fault(struct vm_fault *vmf)
 		goto out_unlock;
 	}
 
-	/* We don't use vmf->pgoff since that has the fake offset: */
-	pgoff = (vmf->address - vma->vm_start) >> PAGE_SHIFT;
+	/*
+	 * vmf->pgoff is the page's offset in the mmap offset space: the
+	 * object's fake offset plus its page index. Taking the index from
+	 * the fault address relative to vm_start would ignore an mmap offset
+	 * into the object (dma-buf mmap at a nonzero offset) and the part of
+	 * a mapping a split or a partial mremap left behind.
+	 */
+	pgoff = vmf->pgoff - drm_vma_node_start(&obj->vma_node);
+	if (GEM_WARN_ON(pgoff >= (obj->size >> PAGE_SHIFT))) {
+		ret = VM_FAULT_SIGBUS;
+		goto out_unlock;
+	}
 
 	pfn = page_to_pfn(pages[pgoff]);
 
